b.add(c,'Using lactose as an energy source','In a simplified bacterial model, a repressor prevents transcription of lactose-utilizing genes when no inducer is present. A lactose-derived inducer binds the repressor.',level='ahl',parts=[P('Explain how the inducer can increase transcription.',R('Binding alters the repressor so it no longer effectively blocks the regulatory DNA site.'),R('RNA polymerase can then transcribe the lactose-utilizing genes.')),P('Explain one advantage of this regulation.',R('The cell avoids making large amounts of unneeded enzymes when their substrate is absent, conserving resources.'))],notes='Bacterial biochemical regulation example; explicitly simplified model, not a requirement to memorize operon nomenclature.')
